{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## RCA (Phase 1 complete — root cause PROVEN)\n\n**Mechanism (confirmed).** `astral-sh/setup-uv` has two independent manifest consumers. Pin 56b7 (`[tool.uv] required-version = \"==0.12.7\"`, commit `7501cc1d`) removed the *version-resolution* fetch (the `==` exact form takes `ExactVersionResolver`, no network). It did **not** remove the *artifact-URL* fetch. On a tool-cache miss, `setupUv` calls `downloadVersion`, whose **first statement is unconditional**:\n\n- `src/download/download-version.ts:42` @ pinned SHA `ae62891` — `const artifact = await getArtifact(version, arch, platform, manifestUrl);` — runs before any branch, regardless of how the version was resolved.\n- `getArtifact → fetchManifest → fetchManifestResponse(VERSIONS_MANIFEST_URL)` (`src/download/manifest.ts`) does the network `fetch()` of `https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/versions/main/v1/uv.ndjson` and emits the `Fetching manifest data from …` line. It is fetched solely to obtain `artifact.downloadUrl`; note that in the default source the **checksum comes from the built-in `KNOWN_CHECKSUMS` table, not the manifest** (confirmed in `download-version.ts`), so only the download URL forces the fetch.\n- A GitHub-hosted runner starts every job with an empty uv tool cache, so `tryGetFromToolCache` always misses → `downloadVersion` always runs → the fetch is guaranteed once per job.\n\n`enable-cache: true` (present at all call sites) caches uv's *package* cache (`~/.cache/uv`), **not** the uv *binary* in the tool cache, so it does not suppress this fetch.\n\n**Proof.**\n- Static: unconditional first-statement call + network fetch, cited above at the pinned SHA (v10.0.0), unchanged in v10.0.1 per ticket.\n- Runtime oracle: the ticket's run 33230196661 log (5 jobs, identical) — `Found version for uv in .../pyproject.toml: 0.12.7` (version from the local pin, no `Could not determine uv version`) yet `Fetching manifest data from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/astral-sh/versions/main/v1/uv.ndjson` still appears. This is the RED signal the ACs demand.\n- Also cited in-repo: `pyproject.toml:326-328` already documents this exact residual (\"the action fetches that manifest a SECOND time, in downloadVersion → getArtifact … unconditional … NOT removed by this pin — see bug 5caa\").\n\n**Legitimacy: defect / incomplete-implementation.** Design authority = 56b7's stated goal \"Pin uv once so CI stops resolving it remotely\" + `scripts/check_uv_pin.py` intent (eliminate the per-job network dependency). The residual fetch violates that goal. **Attribution:** by scope-of-work to **56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc** (`incomplete-implementation` — 56b7 aimed to remove the per-job manifest dependency and completed only the version-resolution half, documenting the rest as out-of-scope). The residual fetch itself is *preexisting* (present since setup-uv adoption), so a closer may alternatively classify `preexisting`. The existing `discovered_from 56b7` edge is recorded; when this closes, pass `--caused-by=56b7-b21a-c8ab-4afc`.\n\n## Scope / blast radius\n25 call sites across 12 workflow files, all pinned at `astral-sh/setup-uv@ae62891 # v10.0.0`. **No `version:` input anywhere** (version resolved from `pyproject.toml`). No composite action exists yet.\n\n## Recommended approach (of the ticket's three, none pre-selected)\n**Approach #2 — a single composite action `.github/actions/setup-uv/action.yml`** that downloads the pinned uv binary directly from the Astral release URL with a **committed sha256** (mirroring the existing `acli` precedent, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md:125-128`), reimplements PATH wiring + optional uv-cache, and replaces every `uses: astral-sh/setup-uv@…` with `uses: ./.github/actions/setup-uv`.\n- Why #2 over #1 (`actions/cache` of the tool cache): #1 only avoids the fetch on a cache **hit** — a cold/evicted cache still runs `downloadVersion` and fetches the manifest, so it cannot robustly satisfy AC-1's \"zero occurrences of `Fetching manifest data`\". #2 removes the manifest read on **every** run, deterministically.\n- Why not #3 (upstream `astral-sh/setup-uv`): correct long-term but not landable now (depends on upstream maintainers + a pin bump).\n- **Residual network dependency (AC-3, named honestly):** #2 still downloads the uv binary from the release/mirror CDN — it removes the *manifest* fetch, not *all* network. The change description must say so; it must not claim \"no network dependency.\"\n\n## Why I am NOT unilaterally landing (escalation)\n1. **Design decision.** The ticket explicitly reserves the approach choice for planning (\"choose ONE … none is pre-selected\"); the three options depend on materially different failure domains / caching / maintenance tradeoffs. Selecting is a behavior/design call, not a mechanical correctness fix.\n2. **Conflict with live epic eb64 (`financial-stoneware-brant`, in_progress, another session).** eb64 declares `file_impact` on `.github/workflows/` (\"Patchset-addressable Jira DC verification wiring\"), which overlaps the exact setup-uv-bearing files any approach must edit: `external-integration.yml`, `gerrit-verify.yaml`, `jira-dc-richtext-probe.yml`, `jira-dc-capability-map.yml`. Landing 25-site workflow edits now would collide.\n\n**Sequencing ask:** confirm approach #2 (or pick another), then land after — or coordinated with — eb64's `.github/workflows/` Jira-DC changes to avoid rebasing over each other. Phase 1 is done and the fix plan is ready; Phase 2 (composite action + RED via a real CI log showing the anchor + zero `Fetching manifest data`) can execute immediately on approval + a clear window."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788066668369536391,"uuid":"c759d6e7-8363-45e8-b530-99af01805ca6"}